  "verbalization": "Bleomycin is linked to TI-73 through a series of molecular interactions involving 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, a compound that acts as a target for multiple proteins, including Lysine-specific demethylase 4C and A388. These proteins are all part of a broader pathway that ultimately directs bleomycin to target TI-73. The evidence suggests that bleomycin's mechanism of action involves a cascade of molecular interactions where the compound is indirectly linked to TI-73 via the 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid pathway. This pathway is a common target for multiple enzymes, indicating a potential for pleiotropic effects. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of bleomycin's interaction with cellular processes, emphasizing the role of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid as a central mediator in the relationship between bleomycin and TI-73.",
